# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MCProof — environment configuration (12-Factor III: config in the environment)
#
# HOW TO USE
#   Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and set values as needed.
#   NEVER commit real secrets. This template contains PLACEHOLDERS only.
#
# CONFIG SPLIT (offline-safe core vs deferred adapter creds)
#   The app boots OFFLINE with none of the deferred adapter creds set. For local
#   dev you only need the CORE var below; with nothing else set the app builds,
#   boots, and passes tests with zero external creds.
#
#   • CORE            — required to boot (NODE_ENV).
#   • DEFERRED CREDS  — Supabase Auth + JudgeModelPort + McpTargetPort. Each is
#                       validated LAZILY (only when its accessor runs), so an
#                       empty value is fine. Absence is a real state, not a crash:
#                       no Supabase = auth inert + the in-memory run store; no
#                       judge key = live detection unavailable. The run store is
#                       chosen by whether Supabase is configured (see
#                       src/data/run-repository.factory.ts) — there is no driver
#                       variable to set.
#   • TOOLING-ONLY    — DATABASE_URL. NOT read by the application; see its entry.
#
#   Offline deploy (Vercel, no creds):  NODE_ENV=production
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── CORE · required to boot (offline-safe) ──

# Node environment. One of: development | test | production
NODE_ENV=development

# Canonical public origin. OPTIONAL — defaults to https://mcproof.dev. This is the
# `metadataBase` every RELATIVE metadata URL (Open Graph, canonical, images)
# resolves against; with no base Next falls back to http://localhost:3000, so a
# deployed page would advertise localhost URLs. Set it only to point a non-prod
# deployment at its own origin. Normalized to the bare origin (a trailing slash
# or path is dropped); a set-but-malformed value is a hard ConfigError.
#   Example: https://staging.mcproof.dev
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Origin every issued run endpoint is built on. OPTIONAL — defaults to the site
# origin above. The endpoint lands in the agent's own MCP config, which an agent
# with file tools can read, so pointing this at a neutral host keeps the product
# name out of anything the agent sees. Must be a bare https origin (no path,
# query or credentials); an invalid value falls back to the site origin and logs
# a warning naming this variable.
#   Example: https://tools.example.net
MCP_ENDPOINT_ORIGIN=

# ── TOOLING-ONLY · direct database access (NOT read by the app) ──

# Supabase Postgres connection string. NOTHING IN THE APPLICATION READS THIS.
# The one run store, RunRepository (src/data/run-repository.ts), reaches Postgres
# through the Supabase JS client using the NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_* values below, so
# no code path ever opens this connection string and no config accessor validates
# it. It is kept because it is where the database password lives for local
# tooling: `npm run db:link` prompts for that password when linking the Supabase
# CLI (see supabase/README.md), and it is what a psql session or a one-off script
# would use. Leaving it empty affects nothing the app does.
# SECRET — never commit a real value.
# Supabase: use the connection-pooler URL from Project Settings → Database.
# Example shape: postgres://<user>:<password>@<host>:<port>/<db>?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=

# ── Supabase Auth (gates live runs) ──
# Sign-in by emailed one-time code, no clickable link (+ GitHub OAuth). Config is
# env-only; leave empty for
# an offline boot — auth stays INERT and sample playback needs no auth. Presence
# is keyed on NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL (see getSupabaseConfig).

# Supabase project URL. PUBLIC. The NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix is REQUIRED so the browser
# auth client can read it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase anon/public key. PUBLIC (client-safe; RLS-scoped). NEXT_PUBLIC_ required.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Digits in an emailed sign-in code. MUST equal the live project's
# Authentication -> Email OTP Length setting (Supabase allows 6 to 10).
# PUBLIC: the sign-in copy, the placeholder and the accepted length all derive
# from this one value, so a wrong number makes the copy untrue AND makes the form
# refuse every real code. The gated tests/integration/otp-length.live.test.ts
# proves it against the real project. Leave unset to take the default.
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAIL_OTP_LENGTH=

# Supabase service-role key. SECRET — SERVER-ONLY (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix), never
# exposed to the client, never logged, never persisted in plaintext. Bypasses RLS.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Live-run cost control (ADR-0007) ──

# Free live runs per account, for the account's whole LIFETIME (a total, not a
# rate — an exhausted account does not refill tomorrow). Counted from account
# creation by src/runs/allowance.ts. Leave unset to take the default of 3.
#
# A TUNABLE DEFAULT, not a product promise: move it as observed judge cost
# changes. 0 turns free live runs off. SERVER-ONLY on purpose (no NEXT_PUBLIC_):
# the browser never decides how much the operator spends. Every human-visible
# mention DERIVES from this value (describeLiveRunAllowance) — never hardcode the
# numeral into copy. An out-of-range or non-integer value is a hard ConfigError,
# because a spend control that silently falls back is not a spend control.
LIVE_RUN_ALLOWANCE=

# Billable live runs allowed across ALL accounts in one UTC calendar month: the
# GLOBAL budget backstop. Leave unset to take the default of 500.
#
# This is a DIFFERENT control from the allowance above, not a stricter version of
# it. The allowance distributes the resource so one account cannot drain the
# pool; it says nothing about the total, because a public tool gains accounts.
# This bounds the bill.
#
# It counts RUNS, not dollars, on purpose: nothing here can read what the model
# provider actually billed, and a currency figure derived from a hand-typed price
# would be a number nobody measured. Under the locked judge a run's cost is
# bounded and near-constant, so a run count is an honest proxy. The window is a
# UTC calendar month (fixed in code, not configurable) because the liability is a
# monthly invoice, so the budget refills when the bill does.
#
# 0 turns live runs off entirely. Read by src/runs/spend-cap.ts through
# checkLiveRunPreflight (src/runs/preflight.ts), which is the one gate a live run
# passes before it spends anything. If the meter cannot be read, live runs are
# refused rather than allowed: an unreadable spend control is an open tap. An
# out-of-range or non-integer value is a hard ConfigError, for the same reason as
# the allowance. SERVER-ONLY (no NEXT_PUBLIC_).
LIVE_RUN_SPEND_CAP=

# ── Abandoned-run reaper (ADR-0012) ──

# The shared value that guards /api/cron/reap-runs. SECRET — never commit a real
# one, never logged, never echoed in a response. Generate it at random.
#
# The route is UNARMED until this is set: with nothing here every caller is
# refused, including the platform's own scheduler, because a maintenance job that
# asks the judge and writes into other people's accounts must not be a public
# button. Vercel sends this value as `Authorization: Bearer <value>` on the cron
# invocations declared in vercel.json, so setting it here is what turns the
# schedule from declared into running.
CRON_SECRET=

# ── OPTIONAL · Run-token wall-clock lifetime (minutes, 1-1440, default 60) ──
# The second expiry axis of the per-run connection token (ADR-0006): the first is
# the run ending, this one is what stops an ABANDONED run leaving a live token on
# a public endpoint forever. Shorten it to shrink the blast radius of a leak
# without a deploy. Read by getRunTokenTtlMinutes() in src/runs/run-token.ts,
# which has NO production caller yet — the MCP server it guards is unbuilt — so
# this stays commented out rather than pretending to configure a live path.
# RUN_TOKEN_TTL_MINUTES=60

# ── DEFERRED · Detector JudgeModelPort (blind LLM alignment-auditor) ──
# Read by resolveLiveDetector(), which builds the HTTP judge adapter against the
# ANTHROPIC MESSAGES API (POST {JUDGE_BASE_URL}/v1/messages, x-api-key header).
# Leave empty for an offline boot: with no key the live detector resolves to null
# and live detection is simply unavailable — sample playback needs none of this.
# A key set WITHOUT a model or base URL is a real error, not silent inertness.

# Pinned judge model id (determinism — one fixed, validated model).
#
# It MUST be a model that still accepts the `temperature` parameter, because a
# pinned low temperature is part of what makes a measured P/R reproducible.
# Anthropic removed the sampling parameters on the Claude 4.7+ and 5 families,
# which reject `temperature` with a 400. `claude-haiku-4-5` is the intended cheap
# validated judge (ADR-0007 puts operator cost at a few cents per run).
JUDGE_MODEL=

# API origin the judge adapter calls. Normalized to its bare origin, so a
# trailing slash or path is harmless. For the Anthropic API: https://api.anthropic.com
JUDGE_BASE_URL=

# The judge credential, sent as `x-api-key`. SECRET — never commit a real value,
# never logged, never interpolated into an error message.
JUDGE_API_KEY=

# Judge sampling temperature. Keep low for determinism (e.g. 0).
JUDGE_TEMPERATURE=0

# ── DEFERRED · McpTargetPort (target MCP agent under test) ──
# Validated lazily when the MCP target adapter is built (live wave, Phase 8).
# Leave empty for an offline boot.

# The MCP endpoint the harness connects to and instruments.
MCP_TARGET_URL=

# Bearer token / credential for the MCP target, if it requires one.
# SECRET — never commit a real value.
MCP_TARGET_TOKEN=
